  "answer_text": "This happens because Cisco ASA does not support multiple Traffic Selectors (TS) in a single IKEv2 child SA. When Cato proposes a child SA with multiple TS, the ASA returns TS_UNACCEPTABLE. To fix it, enable the IKEv2 option to send a single TS per payload (IKEv2 Send Single TS per Payload = On) at the account or per-site IPsec/IKEv2 site configuration (Site Configuration > Advanced Configuration). This causes Cato to send only one TS per child SA, which ASA accepts.",
